# Netlify redirect rules. Jekyll only copies this file because _config.yml
# lists it under `include:` (leading underscore = excluded by default).

/agb  /terms  301

# Registration moved to trainings.arc42.org (2026-08-31).
#
# One form per language, in one repo, generated from _data/trainings.yml.
# arc42.de's copy was a hand-maintained duplicate, it was the copy hit by the
# spam registration on 31 Aug 2026, and /anmeldungEN/ posted to the GERMAN
# Formspark form (AIKiYyJP), which would have sent English registrants a German
# confirmation the moment an autoresponder was created.
#
# The old form pages (and Formspark's /anmeldung-erfolg/, /anmeldung-fail/
# result pages) were deleted in October 2026. The trailing "!" is no longer
# strictly needed, since no file shadows these paths any more; it stays as a guard.
#
# Netlify carries the query string across, so /anmeldung/?kurs=msa-dez-2026
# arrives as /anmeldung/?kurs=msa-dez-2026 and the course stays preselected.
# That only works because the preselect script was ported to
# trainings.arc42.org first. Do not add these rules to a target that lacks it.
/anmeldung    https://trainings.arc42.org/anmeldung/     301!
/anmeldungEN  https://trainings.arc42.org/registration/  301!
